# Trivy suppressions for the finance-app image scan (Issue #131).
#
# The CI gate blocks on HIGH and CRITICAL findings that have a fix available
# (`ignore-unfixed: true`), so an entry here means "we know, and we have
# decided to ship anyway". That decision needs to be reviewable, so every
# entry must carry:
#
#   1. the CVE / advisory ID
#   2. why it does not apply, or why the fix cannot be taken yet
#   3. an expiry date — Trivy honours `exp:` and the finding returns after it
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#   # <why this is suppressed, and what unblocks removing it>
#
# Prefer rebuilding on a patched base image over adding an entry. If a
# suppression outlives two expiry extensions, that is a signal to change the
# base image rather than extend it a third time.
#
# Intentionally empty — populate only from real findings, never pre-emptively.
